# SRG-APP-000097-WSR-000058  -  CAT II
# The web server must produce log records containing sufficient information
# to establish where within the web server the events occurred.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000097-WSR-000058
group:           V-206361
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000132
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    splunkd_access.log names the REST endpoint that handled each request and
                 web_service.log identifies the Splunk Web process that raised each event;
                 the application configures that no endpoint is omitted from the access
                 log.

governs:         restmap.conf - The management interface endpoints, and which clients may reach them.

check:           restmap.conf [] includeInAccessLog not_equals false

external:        The endpoint and process identifiers are written by the product in a fixed
                 record format with no configuration surface, so their content is confirmed
                 by inspecting a written record rather than by reading configuration.

citation:        INVENTION. Removed web.conf [settings] log.error_maxfiles min 1.
                 web.conf.spec defines it as "The maximum number of backup files to keep
                 after the web_service.log file has reached its maximum size" - how many
                 rotated copies are retained, not whether the process identity is recorded.
                 The type is <integer>, so 0 is permitted, and web_service.log is still
                 written at 0; the condition would fail an instance that satisfies the
                 objective. Neither the check nor the fix text concerns log rotation.
finding:         A REST endpoint is configured with includeInAccessLog = false, so requests
                 it handles leave no record in splunkd_access.log and the location within
                 the web server where those events occurred cannot be established.
